#   sk_path_iter - walking an SkPath: SkPath::Iter, SkPath::RawIter and SkPathEdgeIter
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of Skia m144 src/core/SkPath.cpp (lines 295-470: SkPath::Iter, which closes
#       contours with a line back to their start; 470-545: SkPath::RawIter over
#       SkPathPriv::Iterate, which yields the stored verbs with the previous point first),
#       include/core/SkPath.h:1710-1770 (RangeIter) and src/core/SkPathPriv.h:475-570 with
#       src/core/SkPath.cpp:911-927 (SkPathEdgeIter: only the edges, with the closing lines).
